      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Sucks that this is a thing, I am in both Lastation and ERP Enabled and it annoyed me when I saw the jail being just open like that.\n\n-----[Everything past this is a rant]-----\n\n I'd love to report it but at the same time I fear that I'd get punished instead of the people doing this. I often find VRChat staff and rules to be very hypocritical with how it goes about adult content. They say VRC isn't for kids and that the minimum age for access is 13 in the TOS then immediately they turn their backs and start cracking down on any adult content and changing the rules and how they deal with this content and the creators allowing for more children to get in and punishing the creators for posting adult content to an adult platform... it's like if pornhub decided to ban all videos and the creators for containing nudity. It wasn't made for kids, it wasn't indended for kids to be there, and yet for some unknown reason (prolly to keep a high download/player count numbers or VRC+ Sales boosts) they keep Making it more for children when noone really wants this in the first place.\n\nLike make up you fecking minds! Either you want it to be a enjoyable place for adults or children. There's already rec room for kids and you say VRC isn't for kids, So why are you making it easier for children to get it? How about less cracking down on the adult content and focusing on the rampant child outbreak? It's pretty easy to realize that Less children = less problems for VRC. There would be Less pedos, less nuisances in public lobbies, and less problems concerning the visibility of adult content on the platform. If you desperately need those children for numbers sake then perhaps make an 18+ verification for VRC adult content? I don't think it would be too hard to implement an ID verification bot on the VRC website that whitelists the user to show/use the VRC Adult content in a menu like an additional tab.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
