      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Just a quick note. The description of that world shown in the picture says \"Otherwise, you will be banned.\" Is this talking about getting blacklisted from the world?\n\nThe creator guidelines say that you are not allowed to blacklist players from a world. So I would not suggest anyone do that. However, maybe it is an exception if the world isn't actually public?\n\nIf it is eluding to it being against VRChat's terms of service though, then I would suggest rephrasing the description to say this more clearly. For example: \"It is against VRChat's terms of service to make non-private instances of this world.\" Also ensure the world has the correct content warning labels on it.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
