      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{64f7a7a78a0a5323be4cff18|full_name}: Adult content is allowed as long as it is in a private instance and everyone in the instance consent to it. At least that is what the community guidelines were updated to say last year.\n\nBut if the instance is public and anyone can join, then you cannot do this. I don't know the discussed groups, but if they are public groups that allows anyone to join, I would also consider all group and group+ instances belonging to those groups to be public. Maybe this needs to be added to the community guidelines should be updated to specify what a \"private instance\" is, and clearly state that a group instance isn't private if the group allows for players to join it without any moderator having to review the request.\n\nI don't think the content warning labels can be applied to a group, but that would likely be a nice feature for VRChat to implement. Related Canny post: [add-content-gating-to-groups](https://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta/p/add-content-gating-to-groups)",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-09-04T01:46:27.149Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "With the group system Groups are able to make Private worlds public with the `Groups Public` feature... This kind of makes it hard to keep private worlds private.\n\nI have seen a group called (ERP Enabled) \n\nhttps://vrc.group/ERPOK.5125\n\nactively making adult and mature private link only worlds Public and Group+\n\nThis kind of ruins the whole point of making a private world. Sure, they are not searchable but still it's better if Groups can only set private worlds to Group only, at most Group+.",
